01:43:15.972 --> 01:43:19.105
And so watching that
was, like, weird.

01:43:19.758 --> 01:43:22.239
I don't know.
It's weird.

01:43:24.894 --> 01:43:27.201
She really could just be...

01:43:31.553 --> 01:43:33.076
crazy.

01:43:33.642 --> 01:43:34.947
And she said
she didn't wanna be famous,

01:43:34.991 --> 01:43:37.080
she didn't wanna be
in pictures, but like...

01:43:42.085 --> 01:43:44.653
But that's not
the kind of person

01:43:44.696 --> 01:43:47.525
that could create
what she created.

01:43:47.569 --> 01:43:50.006
-What? What kind of person?
-Theranos.

01:43:50.049 --> 01:43:52.095
I think it takes somebody--

01:43:52.138 --> 01:43:54.315
I think
it takes something else.

01:43:55.054 --> 01:43:57.274
-Yeah.
-And I'm sorry, but she did--

01:43:57.318 --> 01:43:59.407
The things
that were frustrating--

01:43:59.450 --> 01:44:00.712
There's a lot of things
that were frustrating,

01:44:00.756 --> 01:44:02.236
and one of them
being that, like,

01:44:02.279 --> 01:44:03.585
Sunny is the bad guy

01:44:03.628 --> 01:44:05.195
and she was just
a victim of Sunny.

01:44:05.239 --> 01:44:06.762
And now she's going to prison.

01:44:06.805 --> 01:44:10.113
It's like, it's-- That's not--

01:44:10.156 --> 01:44:15.161
I mean, is that possible
that Sunny just is the reason?

01:44:16.119 --> 01:44:18.121
Sunny was the guy
lying to people?

01:44:23.474 --> 01:44:25.781
I mean, the challenge
I'm having

01:44:25.824 --> 01:44:27.435
with all of this is

01:44:27.478 --> 01:44:30.264
she was taken away and went in

01:44:30.307 --> 01:44:33.223
and now it's Billy
just saying,

01:44:33.267 --> 01:44:35.007
"I know
what's going on with her."

01:44:35.051 --> 01:44:36.748
And he even said to me, like,

01:44:36.792 --> 01:44:38.533
"I don't even have
to talk to her

01:44:38.576 --> 01:44:39.838
"to know what she wants."

01:44:39.882 --> 01:44:41.623
I wish there was a way
you could find out

01:44:41.666 --> 01:44:44.103
some real shit on Billy,
bring it to her.

01:44:44.147 --> 01:44:45.540
-Find what?
-Break them up.

01:44:46.280 --> 01:44:47.716
You want them to break up?

01:44:47.759 --> 01:44:48.891
No, find some shit on Billy.

01:44:48.934 --> 01:44:50.849
Yeah, of course I do.

01:44:53.548 --> 01:44:55.724
No woman wants to see
another woman go--

01:44:55.767 --> 01:44:58.466
be controlled
by that kind of guy.

01:45:03.253 --> 01:45:04.515
Not that I would do this,

01:45:04.559 --> 01:45:07.344
but I fantasized,
for a minute, like,

01:45:07.388 --> 01:45:10.739
playing her, "post-trial."

01:45:12.480 --> 01:45:14.656
When did you fantasize?

01:45:14.699 --> 01:45:15.874
When I'm--
Just when I was watching--

01:45:15.918 --> 01:45:16.919
Oh, when you were
watching this?

01:45:16.962 --> 01:45:18.529
I forget what scene it was.

01:45:21.619 --> 01:45:23.839
When you were sitting there
on the couch with her...

01:45:24.970 --> 01:45:27.756
[SOFTLY] ..."Good talk",
she's like...

01:45:27.799 --> 01:45:29.018
She's like, what?

01:45:29.061 --> 01:45:30.324
She just--

01:45:31.716 --> 01:45:34.502
Wow. Yeah.

01:45:42.161 --> 01:45:45.687
I feel, like, a--
Feel, like, a little haunted.

01:45:47.166 --> 01:45:51.388
Um, because I have to just sit
with the discomfort of

01:45:51.432 --> 01:45:52.563
A, not knowing,

01:45:52.607 --> 01:45:54.435
and B, not knowing
how I feel about it,

01:45:54.478 --> 01:45:56.872
and C, being able
to do nothing about it,

01:45:56.915 --> 01:45:58.613
and D, just...

01:46:02.007 --> 01:46:05.446
feeling shitty about myself
and my own feelings about it.

01:46:05.489 --> 01:46:07.361
Lots of things.

01:46:07.796 --> 01:46:09.537
She's not just
an idea in my head.

01:46:09.580 --> 01:46:11.930
This shit actually happened.

01:46:17.371 --> 01:46:19.068
AMANDA SEYFRIED: Oh my God.

01:46:19.634 --> 01:46:21.070
[LAUGHS]

01:46:23.855 --> 01:46:26.554
NATHAN: They were, like,
renting it when we shot.

01:46:31.036 --> 01:46:32.864
It's really dusty.

01:46:34.344 --> 01:46:35.867
Were these vitamins here?

01:46:35.911 --> 01:46:36.868
I don't remember that.

01:46:36.912 --> 01:46:38.261
Okay.

01:46:38.304 --> 01:46:40.655
This coffee machine,
for sure, this toaster.

01:46:40.698 --> 01:46:42.526
This, obviously.

01:46:43.005 --> 01:46:44.615
Fridge, microwave.

01:47:37.015 --> 01:47:38.364
Was this here?

01:47:39.409 --> 01:47:40.497
Um...

01:47:41.498 --> 01:47:42.847
I think she used that.

01:47:42.891 --> 01:47:46.938
Or, they had that here.

01:47:46.982 --> 01:47:48.723
She didn't really
drink coffee.

01:47:52.640 --> 01:47:54.903
-Um...
-Do you miss her?

01:47:59.037 --> 01:48:00.474
Miss? I mean...

01:48:02.388 --> 01:48:03.825
It must be weird.

01:48:10.266 --> 01:48:12.398
I don't know,
miss is a weird word.

01:48:17.403 --> 01:48:21.103
Can I tell you something

01:48:21.669 --> 01:48:22.974
or a story about how this,

01:48:23.018 --> 01:48:24.759
like, something
that happened here,

01:48:24.802 --> 01:48:28.414
that I still sort of,
think about?

01:48:28.850 --> 01:48:30.286
Yeah.

01:48:33.071 --> 01:48:35.334
It was before
we had cameras here.

01:48:35.378 --> 01:48:36.640
It sort of--

01:48:38.642 --> 01:48:42.254
it sort of relates to how
this whole project came about.

01:48:43.952 --> 01:48:45.127
Like, when you first met?

01:48:45.170 --> 01:48:46.389
NATHAN: Yeah.

01:48:47.346 --> 01:48:49.653
Basically, I went down
to meet her

01:48:49.697 --> 01:48:52.787
and Billy for the first time,
in San Diego,

01:48:52.830 --> 01:48:55.703
after I heard a rumor
through the grapevine

01:48:55.746 --> 01:49:00.403
that maybe she was interested
in having her life documented.

01:49:00.446 --> 01:49:02.144
You sure
you don't want any oatmeal?

01:49:02.187 --> 01:49:03.580
I'm all right. Thanks.

01:49:04.233 --> 01:49:06.452
I took notes after
on everything that happened.

01:49:06.496 --> 01:49:07.932
And so this script is sort of

01:49:07.976 --> 01:49:09.455
-based on...
-Right.

01:49:09.499 --> 01:49:11.414
...my memory of what happened

01:49:11.457 --> 01:49:14.069
and like, those notes I had.

01:49:14.112 --> 01:49:16.158
Billy showed me
a clip of something

01:49:16.201 --> 01:49:17.855
that you made on YouTube.

01:49:17.899 --> 01:49:20.466
You were at a gas station
talking to the owner.

01:49:21.555 --> 01:49:25.210
Oh, yeah, that was from
a comedy show I used to make

01:49:25.254 --> 01:49:27.386
called Nathan For You.

01:49:27.430 --> 01:49:30.999
It was pretty clear
from the moment I met her

01:49:31.042 --> 01:49:33.741
that she had no real clue
who I was

01:49:33.784 --> 01:49:37.092
or had seen anything
I had made before.

01:49:37.135 --> 01:49:39.094
And then she asked
if you had kids.

01:49:39.137 --> 01:49:40.574
Do you have kids?

01:49:40.617 --> 01:49:41.618
No.

01:49:43.359 --> 01:49:45.927
It's completely changed me.

01:49:48.016 --> 01:49:49.713
-Good.
-I think you'd be great at it.

01:49:49.757 --> 01:49:51.410
Great at what?

01:49:51.454 --> 01:49:53.108
Being a dad.

01:49:53.891 --> 01:49:55.589
-Which was...
-NATHAN: Yeah.

01:49:55.632 --> 01:49:56.807
...so bizarre.

01:49:56.851 --> 01:49:58.330
I don't know. It was weird

01:49:58.374 --> 01:49:59.810
because like,
when she said that,

01:49:59.854 --> 01:50:02.857
it actually, like, made me
feel good, for some reason.

01:50:02.900 --> 01:50:04.859
-[EXCLAIMS SOFTLY]
-It felt super sincere.

01:50:04.902 --> 01:50:06.251
But, because
I was feeling that,

01:50:06.295 --> 01:50:08.166
that weird mix of

01:50:08.819 --> 01:50:10.386
this feels so authentic
with her,

01:50:10.429 --> 01:50:11.996
but then I don't trust it,

01:50:12.040 --> 01:50:13.911
it felt like watching
a magician.

01:50:15.609 --> 01:50:16.784
Do you know
who David Blaine is,

01:50:16.827 --> 01:50:18.046
the magician?

01:50:18.089 --> 01:50:19.264
[LAUGHS SOFTLY]

01:50:19.569 --> 01:50:20.614
I do.

01:50:20.657 --> 01:50:22.137
And that just came
to your mind?

01:50:22.180 --> 01:50:23.878
Yeah. In the moment.

01:50:23.921 --> 01:50:25.706
And I wrote, this is basically
verbatim, what I told her.

01:50:25.749 --> 01:50:26.968
Yeah.

01:50:27.795 --> 01:50:29.448
All right, so David Blaine
does this thing

01:50:29.492 --> 01:50:32.451
where he sticks an ice pick

01:50:32.495 --> 01:50:34.192
right through the palm
of his hand.

01:50:35.280 --> 01:50:38.849
And, the way he presents it,
it looks like a magic trick.

01:50:39.371 --> 01:50:41.199
But I actually think
he's really sticking

01:50:41.243 --> 01:50:42.810
the ice pick through his hand.

01:50:42.853 --> 01:50:44.507
Like I saw in an interview,
he said he, like,

01:50:44.550 --> 01:50:46.552
dug a tiny hole
through his hand

01:50:46.596 --> 01:50:49.077
so it, like,
actually is going through.

01:50:49.120 --> 01:50:51.906
But, it will-- It always just
looks like a trick to people,

01:50:51.949 --> 01:50:53.908
'cause of how he presents it.

01:50:55.779 --> 01:50:58.564
And what I find
so interesting about you,

01:50:58.608 --> 01:51:00.218
is that in the aftermath
of everything

01:51:00.262 --> 01:51:01.742
that's happened with you,

01:51:01.785 --> 01:51:04.092
with the reputation you have,

01:51:04.135 --> 01:51:05.963
no offense, but I--

01:51:06.007 --> 01:51:09.837
I don't think anyone will ever
believe you ever again.

01:51:09.880 --> 01:51:11.055
Like, you could be
telling the truth

01:51:11.099 --> 01:51:12.840
as much as you want

01:51:12.883 --> 01:51:14.929
and just no one's
gonna believe you.

01:51:14.972 --> 01:51:17.583
So when I said that to her,
I remember her eyes lit up.

01:51:17.627 --> 01:51:20.543
And she was, like,
very excited by this idea.

01:51:20.586 --> 01:51:24.634
And you're not really saying
that it's like, a good thing.

01:51:24.678 --> 01:51:25.896
No.

01:51:25.940 --> 01:51:27.463
And she's, like,
she's taking credit.

01:51:27.506 --> 01:51:29.944
Billy, did you hear
what Nathan just said?

01:51:29.987 --> 01:51:31.423
No. What'd he say?

01:51:31.467 --> 01:51:33.208
He said I'm like--

01:51:33.251 --> 01:51:35.123
I remind him of David Blaine.

01:51:36.037 --> 01:51:37.647
NATHAN: She sort of
paraphrased what I had said.

01:51:37.691 --> 01:51:40.824
And, then they had
this weird look

01:51:40.868 --> 01:51:42.217
between each other.

01:51:42.260 --> 01:51:44.436
Like the two of them shared
this knowing look.

01:51:44.480 --> 01:51:45.655
And I was like, what?

01:51:45.699 --> 01:51:47.701
Billy said that--

01:51:48.614 --> 01:51:51.530
that your mind works
in interesting ways.

01:51:53.402 --> 01:51:54.620
Okay.

01:51:55.578 --> 01:51:58.842
We only wanna
let people into our lives

01:51:58.886 --> 01:52:00.496
who think outside the box.

01:52:00.539 --> 01:52:02.933
And you look at things
differently.

01:52:02.977 --> 01:52:06.589
And you don't give a fuck
what people think.

01:52:07.764 --> 01:52:10.549
So after that, things came
together really quickly.

01:52:10.593 --> 01:52:12.203
We basically went
from that first meeting

01:52:12.247 --> 01:52:13.770
to coming down to shoot

01:52:13.814 --> 01:52:15.641
in the San Diego house
they were renting...

01:52:15.685 --> 01:52:16.773
-Yeah.
-...within a week.

01:52:16.817 --> 01:52:18.340
-Oh my God.
-Yeah.

01:52:18.383 --> 01:52:19.471
AMANDA: Wow.

01:52:19.515 --> 01:52:20.603
NATHAN: There was
this urgency

01:52:20.646 --> 01:52:21.865
to get started
with the project

01:52:21.909 --> 01:52:24.781
because she was going
to prison soon.

01:52:24.825 --> 01:52:26.565
So we began filming with them

01:52:26.609 --> 01:52:30.265
before she had signed
any appearance release.

01:52:30.700 --> 01:52:32.397
Uh-oh.

01:52:32.441 --> 01:52:34.922
NATHAN: But the thing that
I can't get out of my head

01:52:34.965 --> 01:52:37.315
is something that happened
at this meeting

01:52:37.359 --> 01:52:39.491
that Billy
said he wanted to have

01:52:39.535 --> 01:52:41.798
before they agreed to sign
anything.

01:52:41.842 --> 01:52:42.973
[DOORBELL RINGING]

01:52:43.408 --> 01:52:45.715
He requested we come
to their friend's house in LA.

01:52:45.759 --> 01:52:46.803
-Hey.
-NATHAN: Hi.

01:52:46.847 --> 01:52:48.370
-They're in the kitchen.
-Okay, great.

01:52:48.413 --> 01:52:52.113
NATHAN: It was me, Lance,
the co-director of this,

01:52:52.156 --> 01:52:54.637
and two executives from A24.

01:52:54.680 --> 01:52:57.858
And we all sat
around this table.

01:52:57.901 --> 01:53:00.774
And Liz started reading
the opening chapter

01:53:00.817 --> 01:53:03.211
to this, I guess, a book,
she was writing.

01:53:03.254 --> 01:53:06.780
The first chapter I'm calling,
"Waking Up".

01:53:07.998 --> 01:53:10.566
"Love ignites a courage
that cannot be extinguished.

01:53:10.609 --> 01:53:12.394
"The sheets in our bed
are so soft.

01:53:12.437 --> 01:53:14.222
"I roll over and look at you.

01:53:14.526 --> 01:53:16.006
"You are perfect.

01:53:16.050 --> 01:53:17.486
"Your arms are wrapped
over my heart."

01:53:17.529 --> 01:53:18.879
NATHAN: We all--
We didn't know what

01:53:18.922 --> 01:53:20.141
the reason
for the meeting was...

01:53:20.184 --> 01:53:21.403
-AMANDA: Right.
-so when she started

01:53:21.446 --> 01:53:22.883
reading it,

01:53:22.926 --> 01:53:24.841
we were like,
oh, is there a point to this?

01:53:25.624 --> 01:53:27.061
I wouldn't say

01:53:27.104 --> 01:53:28.671
-she's a writer, but--
-Yeah.

01:53:28.714 --> 01:53:30.325
"Every time I saw the beams
falling through our windows,

01:53:30.368 --> 01:53:33.589
"I was one with my dad,
from the moment I was born."

01:53:33.632 --> 01:53:36.592
-That's-- That's it. So far.
-Wow.

01:53:36.635 --> 01:53:38.376
-Wow.
-Awesome.

01:53:38.420 --> 01:53:39.638
EXECUTIVE 1: So, so, so great.

01:53:39.682 --> 01:53:40.944
LANCE: Fantastic.
EXECUTIVE 2: Incredible.

01:53:40.988 --> 01:53:42.554
-EXECUTIVE 1: So good. Really.
-Thank you.

01:53:42.598 --> 01:53:45.253
So you guys are all saying
how great it is.

01:53:45.296 --> 01:53:46.471
Well we were trying
to be polite.

01:53:46.515 --> 01:53:47.821
-Absolutely.
-I didn't know

01:53:47.864 --> 01:53:49.170
-really what to say. Yeah.
-For sure. Of course.

01:53:49.213 --> 01:53:50.998
[CHILDREN CHATTERING]

01:53:51.041 --> 01:53:52.173
NATHAN: And then
you could hear

01:53:52.216 --> 01:53:54.392
her oldest child,
like, sort of

01:53:54.436 --> 01:53:56.612
yelling and playing
in another room.

01:53:56.655 --> 01:53:57.787
AMANDA: Yeah.

01:53:57.831 --> 01:53:59.049
NATHAN: So she gets up
in that moment

01:53:59.093 --> 01:54:02.009
from the table
and goes to see the kids.

01:54:04.446 --> 01:54:05.621
BILLY ACTOR: Okay.

01:54:07.536 --> 01:54:11.583
So, guys, I think we need
to have a conversation

01:54:11.627 --> 01:54:15.979
about the terms of our
involvement in this project.

01:54:18.068 --> 01:54:21.767
Okay, what do you--
what do you mean by that?

01:54:21.811 --> 01:54:23.421
Once she was gone,

01:54:23.465 --> 01:54:25.249
Billy started talking
about money.

01:54:25.293 --> 01:54:26.468
I don't know
what your vision is

01:54:26.511 --> 01:54:28.078
for this project.

01:54:28.818 --> 01:54:32.039
Okay, you guys are artists
and that's what drives you.

01:54:32.082 --> 01:54:34.041
But I do know
that there is potential

01:54:34.084 --> 01:54:36.652
for this movie
to also make a lot of money

01:54:37.174 --> 01:54:38.523
and...

01:54:42.049 --> 01:54:45.139
I feel strongly that

01:54:45.182 --> 01:54:47.706
if this movie
were to make money,

01:54:48.707 --> 01:54:51.667
that we should be entitled
to some of it.

01:54:51.710 --> 01:54:53.060
Which is not customary
and just...

01:54:53.103 --> 01:54:55.149
-No.
-...kind of unethical.

01:54:55.192 --> 01:54:58.804
It's not customary for people
to make a profit

01:54:58.848 --> 01:55:01.329
off of documentaries
that they're appearing in.

01:55:01.372 --> 01:55:03.070
I mean I was vocal
with him too.

01:55:03.113 --> 01:55:04.636
-AMANDA: Yeah.
-I said--

01:55:04.680 --> 01:55:06.551
I agree with Ravi
on this completely.

01:55:06.595 --> 01:55:08.510
It is not a good idea.

01:55:09.119 --> 01:55:10.294
But why, Nathan?

01:55:10.338 --> 01:55:12.166
I mean,
the optics are terrible.

01:55:12.209 --> 01:55:14.646
If you guys are making money
from this documentary,

01:55:14.690 --> 01:55:16.387
people are gonna question
your guys' motives

01:55:16.431 --> 01:55:18.433
for being in it
in the first place.

01:55:18.476 --> 01:55:22.263
And also,
it might give the perception

01:55:22.306 --> 01:55:25.179
that you guys have
a creative say

01:55:25.222 --> 01:55:26.832
over what
the final product is.

01:55:26.876 --> 01:55:29.705
This is not--
It's not good for the film.

01:55:29.748 --> 01:55:31.011
BILLY ACTOR: No,
but I've looked into this,

01:55:31.054 --> 01:55:33.578
and there are many,
many examples

01:55:33.622 --> 01:55:36.277
of documentary subjects
getting paid.

01:55:36.320 --> 01:55:37.756
The Meghan Markle

01:55:37.800 --> 01:55:38.975
and Prince Harry documentary
on Netflix,

01:55:39.019 --> 01:55:40.324
I read somewhere
that they got paid

01:55:40.368 --> 01:55:41.717
$100 million to make that.

01:55:41.760 --> 01:55:43.545
That's not
a real documentary, Billy.

01:55:43.588 --> 01:55:45.460
I know, but Lance--
I know it's bad,

01:55:45.503 --> 01:55:48.115
but the fact is that
they did get paid for that.

01:55:48.158 --> 01:55:49.943
AMANDA: But then it ends...

01:55:50.465 --> 01:55:52.249
It's a non-negotiable.

01:55:52.293 --> 01:55:53.642
...with him eating
a slice of pizza.

01:55:53.685 --> 01:55:56.471
NATHAN: Yeah, I guess
the friend had got pizza

01:55:56.514 --> 01:55:57.776
for this meeting.

01:55:57.820 --> 01:55:59.953
So there was, like,
several pizzas there.

01:56:00.823 --> 01:56:03.608
Um, like, what did you decide?

01:56:04.696 --> 01:56:08.135
Well, at this point, like,
he had all the leverage,

01:56:08.178 --> 01:56:11.747
so, A24 felt they had, like,
no choice but to give him

01:56:11.790 --> 01:56:13.270
